; dsv4-layer-q8q2-band.bml -- ONE DeepSeek-V4 layer's forward on the Metal door, in the tensor types of the REAL IQ2XXS file, against the oracle's own layer arithmetic: the three blocks (ratio 0 hashed,
; ratio 4 and ratio 2 with the biased top-k, and the compressor; every dense projection Q8_0, every gate and up stack IQ2_XXS, every down stack Q2_K at a hidden width of 256) on the SECOND fixture
; (dsv4-fixture-gguf.fk dfx-v-write), every stage of the attention half and the FFN half, over eight positions, alone and chained with the same gates as dsv4-layer-band.bml. The only things that moved
; are the fixture and the claims that were pinned to the first fixture's weights (the softplus stage maxima, the clamp's bite); each tensor is read by the type its own table row carries.
;
; WHAT THIS PINS. native/metal/dsv4-layer.fk enqueues one block at one position over the handles dsv4-open.fk opened (hc_pre, the MLA half with the compressor, hc_post, the FFN half). This band
; opens the fixture it writes under temp_dir (1,778,144 bytes) at capacity 8, writes the two rope tables, and runs eight tokens (5, 17, 3, 22, 9, 28, 14, 1) through the three blocks two ways:
;   ALONE   each block is fed the REFERENCE's own input at that position (the previous block's fp64 output, rounded to f32 by the write), so one block's disagreement is its own and does not compound
;           (the oracle harness's THIS-LAYER-ALONE gate: nd = max|gpu - ref| / max|ref| below the 3e-5 floor of max(8 ne, 3e-5), metal_dsv4_stack_oracle.sh above cmpOra, history 8a6f123d3^);
;   CHAINED the GPU feeds itself (block 0 -> 1 -> 2 at each position, its own residual and its own caches), held to the chain gate max(8 x 1.4e-5, 3e-5) = 1.12e-4.
; The reference is dsv4-oracle-reference.bml (dfo-attention-half, dfo-ffn: fp64, independent of every production MLA/HC/MoE recipe) on the same file, with the raw KV history it keeps, threaded here.
; THE ONE LEG THE ORACLE DOES NOT HAVE IS THE COMPRESSOR. The oracle holds no compressed lane. Its attention is the arithmetic of a union of rows, so the reference gives it the raw history plus the
; compressed rows the author twin dsv4-compressor.fk produces (the twin's pool and norm, then the oracle's own rotation at comp_pos with the compressed base and YaRN ramp, then the oracle's own fp8+f16
; round). The compressed legs (block 1 at positions 3 and 7, block 2 at positions 1 to 7) are therefore pinned to the TWIN, not to an independent oracle: a wrong compressor recipe that the twin shares
; would pass. Everything else in the reference is the oracle's.
;
; Verdict 4095 when every claim lands:
;   1     the cell and its refusals: every block of the fixture is supported; the dispatch counts are pinned (block 0: attention 22, FFN 19 with three routing dispatches; blocks 1 and 2: FFN 18, attention
;         25 a token of which the compressor's state work is 3, and 6 more (ratio 4) or 5 more (ratio 2) at a boundary); a position at the capacity, a block out of range and a ratio-4 block at position
;         2048 each answer nothing and touch no buffer (a sentinel in the output stays)
;   2     block 0 (hashed routing, ratio 0, IQ2_XXS gate and up with Q2_K down experts) alone at positions 0 to 7, KV growing 1 to 8 rows: xn, the roped query, the cached row, the attention heads (inverse roped), output_a, attn_out,
;         the post-attention streams, ffn_cur, ffn_norm, the router logits, the experts the hash table names (exactly), the router weights, the shared expert, the FFN sum and the output streams, each in the gate
;   4     block 1 (biased top-k, ratio 4, IQ2_XXS gate and up with Q2_K down experts, the -1e30 sentinel expert refused) alone at positions 0 to 2: the compressed lane is empty there, so this leg is the oracle's alone, stage for stage
;   8     block 2 (biased top-k, ratio 2) alone at position 0, the same
;   16    the compressor legs, against the oracle's arithmetic over the twin's rows: block 1 at position 3 (the first compressed row, attention over 4 raw + 1 compressed) and block 2 at positions 1 to 3
;         (rows 1 and 2), every stage in the gate, and the compressed arena itself (rotated, rounded rows) equal to the reference's rows
;   32    chained: the GPU feeds itself through the three blocks at eight positions, each block's output streams against the reference chain within the chain gate; every disagreement is printed
;   64    the checks can fail: at each compressed row (block 1 at 3 and 7, block 2 at 1, 3, 5 and 7) the reference WITHOUT the row reads far from the GPU's attention heads (so the compressed legs witness
;         the lane), at position 7 of block 1 the rows an UNSHIFTED twin would give read far from the GPU's two compressed rows (so the second window witnesses the shift), a block fed an input tilted
;         by 1e-4 reads outside the gate, and a block fed through the embedding path agrees with the reference's own embedding input exactly
;   128   release: dsv4-close in synced rounds leaves no handle and metal_live reads what it read before the open
;   256   the second windows, positions 4 to 7 of blocks 1 and 2 alone: block 1's second ratio-4 window (position 7) pools over the state comp_shift left, so a launch that shifts nothing or too little
;         reads wrong there; block 2 emits at 5 and 7 as well as 1 and 3; every stage in the gate, the compressed arena (two rows on block 1, four on block 2) equal to the twin's
;   512   the clamp is wired per block: dkl-clamp reads 10.0, 1.0, 2.0 from the header, equal to the fixture's own metadata (dfo-meta) on each block; the oracle's own mid equals the clamped one on blocks 1
;         and 2 and the clamp changes nothing on block 0 (lim 10.0); how much it bites on this fixture's activations is printed (the first fixture's band holds the bite)
;   1024  the type wiring can fail, on the layer's own dispatch path: with the Q2_K id kernel's scale nibble read as the min (sc / 16 where q2k_umod(sc, 16) stands), with the Q8_0 lane's block stride 33 where
;         34 stand, and with the IQ2_XXS kernel routed to a Q2_K stack, each planted pipeline put in the context under the real kernel's name for one block run (block 1 at position 0, block 0 at position 0),
;         the block reads OUTSIDE the gate; the control (the unplanted kernel) and the restored kernel read inside it. The first fixture's own claim 1024 (the router's softplus against stage maxima pinned on
;         THAT fixture's weights) is not repeated: its numbers belong to its weights
;   2048  an expert type no kernel reads is a refusal, never a neighbour's kernel: dkl-expert-kernel names the three kernels for types 40, 16 and 10 and reads nothing for 12, 41, 8, 0 or -1; with block 1's
;         down stack retyped 12 in the context's own view record for one run, dkl-supported? refuses the block, dsv4-layer-ffn answers nothing, dkl-experts (called past admission) answers [0] and
;         enqueues none of its dispatches (the expert and stream buffers keep their sentinel); with the view restored the same calls read supported and four enqueues
;
; PROOF LEVEL: FOURTH-ARM ONLY -- every bit needs a live Metal device behind the handle door; the fixture is written and read as a binary file. Light GPU: 24 block runs of a few hundred threads over a 1.5 MB
; fixture, one tilted run, a chained pass of 24 more. Never maps a model; writes only under temp_dir and removes what it made.
// preludes: form-stdlib/core.fk form-stdlib/str-byte-at.fk form-stdlib/equireach.fk form-stdlib/gguf-manifest.fk form-stdlib/dsv4-fixture-gguf.fk form-stdlib/dsv4-layout.fk native/metal/dsv4-bind.fk form-stdlib/dsv4-kernels.fk native/metal/dsv4-open.fk native/metal/dsv4-layer.fk form-stdlib/dsv4-compressor.fk form-stdlib/f16-decode.fk form/form-stdlib/bml/dsv4-oracle-reference.bml
section [form.bml] {
 class Dsv4LayerQ8q2Band {
  def dql-bit(held, bit) = held ? bit : 0;
  def dql-tokens() = [5, 17, 3, 22, 9, 28, 14, 1];
  def dql-chain-bound() = 0.000112;
  def dql-ratio(c, il) = dvl-l(record_get(c, "m"), il, "ratio");
  def dql-hd(c) = record_get(record_get(c, "m"), "hd");
  def dql-nrot(c) = record_get(record_get(c, "m"), "nrot");
  def dql-eps() = 0.000001;
  def dql-pre(il) = "blk." ++ il.str() ++ ".";
  def dql-ctx(c) = record_get(c, "ctx");
  def dql-rd(ctx, name, n) = dkr-read(dso-buf(ctx, name), n);
  def dql-flat(rows) = len(rows) == 0 ? [] : append(rows[0], dql-flat(rows[1:]));
  def dql-ape-rows(r, key, k, n) = k == n ? [] : append(dfo-plain(r, key, k), dql-ape-rows(r, key, k + 1, n));

  // ---- the reference: the oracle's layer over a raw history and the compressed rows of the twin ----------------------------------------------
  // a block's reference state is [raw rows, compressed rows, twin state]; the twin state is nothing on a block without a compressor
  // the state of one block is [raw rows, compressed rows, twin state, the same twin WITHOUT the ratio-4 shift, the compressed rows that unshifted twin gives]; the last two exist only to witness
  // that the second ratio-4 window reads the shifted state (the unshifted twin's second row reads far from the shifted one)
  def dql-ls-new(c, il) {
   let ratio = dql-ratio(c, il);
   let tw = ratio == 0 ? nothing() : dcp-state-new(ratio, dql-hd(c));
   [[], [], tw, ratio == 4 ? tw : nothing(), []];
  }
  // the twin's inputs at this position: its two F16 projections of attn_norm come from the oracle's own matrix reader; [kv_cur, sc_cur, ape, norm weight]
  def dql-comp-inputs(c, il, pos, resid) {
   let r = record_get(c, "r");
   let g = record_get(c, "g");
   let p = dql-pre(il);
   let pre = dfo-hc-pre(r, p, "attn", resid, g);
   let xn = dnr-rms-weight(record_get(pre, "cur"), dfo-plain(r, p ++ "attn_norm.weight", 0), dql-eps());
   [dfo-f16-matrix(r, p ++ "attn_compressor_kv.weight", xn), dfo-f16-matrix(r, p ++ "attn_compressor_gate.weight", xn), dql-ape-rows(r, p ++ "attn_compressor_ape.weight", 0, dql-ratio(c, il)), dfo-plain(r, p ++ "attn_compressor_norm.weight", 0)];
  }
  // dcp-step's own law minus the shift after a ratio-4 compression: the wrong answer the second window would read if comp_shift did nothing
  def dql-step-unshifted(s, ratio, hd, pos, inp) {
   let s1 = dcp-update(s, ratio, hd, pos, inp[0], inp[1], inp[2]);
   dcp-compress?(ratio, pos) == 0 ? [s1, []] : [s1, dcp-norm(dcp-pool(s1, ratio, hd), inp[3], dql-eps())];
  }
  // the twin's normed pooled row, rotated at comp_pos with the compressed table by the oracle's own factors and rounded by the oracle's own fp8+f16 round
  def dql-comp-row(c, il, pos, normed) {
   let r = record_get(c, "r");
   let ratio = dql-ratio(c, il);
   dfo-kv-round(dfo-rope-heads(normed, dql-hd(c), dql-nrot(c), dfo-rope-factors(dfo-rope-params(r, il), dql-nrot(c), pos + 1 - ratio, 0)), dql-hd(c), dql-nrot(c));
  }
  // one block: [a, f, out, raw rows after, compressed rows after, twin state after, raw rows before, compressed rows before, unshifted compressed rows after, unshifted twin after]
  def dql-ref-layer(c, il, pos, token, resid, ls) {
   let r = record_get(c, "r");
   let g = record_get(c, "g");
   let ratio = dql-ratio(c, il);
   let inp = ratio == 0 ? nothing() : dql-comp-inputs(c, il, pos, resid);
   let step = ratio == 0 ? nothing() : dcp-step(ls[2], ratio, dql-hd(c), pos, inp[0], inp[1], inp[2], inp[3], dql-eps());
   let stepN = ratio == 4 ? dql-step-unshifted(ls[3], ratio, dql-hd(c), pos, inp) : nothing();
   let emitted = (ratio == 0 || len(step[1]) == 0) ? false : true;
   let emittedN = (ratio != 4 || len(stepN[1]) == 0) ? false : true;
   let comp1 = emitted ? append(ls[1], [dql-comp-row(c, il, pos, step[1])]) : ls[1];
   let compN1 = emittedN ? append(ls[4], [dql-comp-row(c, il, pos, stepN[1])]) : ls[4];
   let a = dfo-attention-half(r, dql-pre(il), resid, g, il, pos, append(ls[0], comp1));
   let f = dfo-ffn(r, dql-pre(il), record_get(a, "after_attn_hc"), g, token, il);
   [a, f, record_get(f, "out_hc"), append(ls[0], [record_get(a, "kv")]), comp1, ratio == 0 ? nothing() : step[0], ls[0], ls[1], compN1, ratio == 4 ? stepN[0] : nothing()];
  }
  def dql-ref-layers(c, pos, token, lss, il, resid) = il == 3 ? [[], []] : {
   let lr = dql-ref-layer(c, il, pos, token, resid, lss[il]);
   let rest = dql-ref-layers(c, pos, token, lss, il + 1, lr[2]);
   [cons(lr, rest[0]), cons([lr[3], lr[4], lr[5], lr[9], lr[8]], rest[1])];
  };
  // over the positions: [resid0, [block records]] each
  def dql-ref-run(c, pos, lss) = pos == len(dql-tokens()) ? [] : {
   let r = record_get(c, "r");
   let embed = dfo-plain(r, "token_embd.weight", dql-tokens()[pos]);
   let resid0 = dnr-flat(dnr-fill(4, embed));
   let layers = dql-ref-layers(c, pos, dql-tokens()[pos], lss, 0, resid0);
   cons([resid0, layers[0]], dql-ref-run(c, pos + 1, layers[1]));
  };
  def dql-ref-start(c) = dql-ref-run(c, 0, [dql-ls-new(c, 0), dql-ls-new(c, 1), dql-ls-new(c, 2)]);
  def dql-lr(ref, pos, il) = ref[pos][1][il];
  def dql-input(ref, pos, il) = il == 0 ? ref[pos][0] : ref[pos][1][il - 1][2];

  // ---- one block run against its reference -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  def dql-attn-triples(ctx, a) = [["xn", dql-rd(ctx, "xn", 256), record_get(a, "xn")], ["q", dql-rd(ctx, "q-n", 256), record_get(a, "q")], ["kv", dql-rd(ctx, "kv-q", 128), record_get(a, "kv")],
   ["heads", dql-rd(ctx, "heads", 256), record_get(a, "heads")], ["low", dql-rd(ctx, "low", 64), record_get(a, "low")], ["attn_out", dql-rd(ctx, "attn-out", 256), record_get(a, "attn_out")],
   ["after_attn", dql-rd(ctx, "resid-next", 1024), record_get(a, "after_attn_hc")]];
  def dql-ffn-triples(ctx, f) = [["ffn_cur", dql-rd(ctx, "hc-cur", 256), record_get(f, "ffn_cur")], ["ffn_norm", dql-rd(ctx, "xn", 256), record_get(f, "ffn_norm")],
   ["logits", dql-rd(ctx, "router-logits", 4), record_get(f, "router_logits")], ["w", dql-rd(ctx, "expert-weights", 2), record_get(f, "expert_w")], ["shared", dql-rd(ctx, "shared-down", 256), record_get(f, "shared")],
   ["ffn_out", dql-rd(ctx, "ffn-out", 256), record_get(f, "ffn_out")], ["out_hc", dql-rd(ctx, "resid", 1024), record_get(f, "out_hc")]];
  def dql-nds(ts) = len(ts) == 0 ? [] : cons(dkr-nd(ts[0][1], ts[0][2]), dql-nds(ts[1:]));
  def dql-labels(ts, nds) = len(ts) == 0 ? "" : (ts[0][0] ++ " " ++ nds[0].str() ++ "  " ++ dql-labels(ts[1:], nds[1:]));
  def dql-below(nds, bound) = len(nds) == 0 ? true : (nds[0] < bound && dql-below(nds[1:], bound));
  def dql-read-ids(ctx) = dkr-read-u32(dso-buf(ctx, "expert-ids"), 2);
  def dql-write-resid(ctx, xs) = metal_buf_write(dso-buf(ctx, "resid"), 0, dkr-f32-bytes(xs));
  // the embedding path of block 0's input: the token's row, broadcast to the four streams
  def dql-embed-in(ctx, token) {
   let e1 = dkr-go(dso-pipe(ctx, "form_dsv4_embed_f16"), [dso-handle(ctx, "token_embd.weight"), dso-buf(ctx, "hc-cur")], [token, 256], 256);
   let e2 = dkr-go(dso-pipe(ctx, "form_hc_broadcast_f32"), [dso-buf(ctx, "hc-cur"), dso-buf(ctx, "resid")], [4, 256], 1024);
   e1 == 1 && e2 == 1;
  }
  // at an emission position keep the disagreement the reference WITHOUT the compressed row would show against the GPU's heads (the falsifier of the compressed legs)
  def dql-noted(c, fal, il, pos, input, lr, heads) {
   let ratio = dql-ratio(c, il);
   (ratio > 0 && (pos + 1) % ratio == 0) ? record_set(fal, "nc-" ++ il.str() ++ "-" ++ pos.str(), dkr-nd(heads, record_get(dfo-attention-half(record_get(c, "r"), dql-pre(il), input, record_get(c, "g"), il, pos, lr[6]), "heads"))) : 0;
  }
  // the block il at pos against lr, fed `input` (a list of 1024 f32, or nothing: the embedding path); sts holds that block's caches
  def dql-run(c, label, il, pos, input, lr, sts, fal) {
   let ctx = dql-ctx(c);
   let token = dql-tokens()[pos];
   let fed = nothing?(input) ? dql-embed-in(ctx, token) : (dql-write-resid(ctx, input) >= 0);
   let n1 = dsv4-layer-attn(ctx, sts, il, pos, 8);
   let s1 = metal_sync();
   let ta = dql-attn-triples(ctx, lr[0]);
   let nda = dql-nds(ta);
   let heads = dql-rd(ctx, "heads", 256);
   let n2 = dsv4-layer-ffn(ctx, il, token);
   let s2 = metal_sync();
   let tf = dql-ffn-triples(ctx, lr[1]);
   let ndf = dql-nds(tf);
   let ids = dql-read-ids(ctx);
   let refIds = record_get(lr[1], "selected");
   let ncomp = dql-ratio(c, il) == 0 ? 0 : (pos + 1) / dql-ratio(c, il);
   let compNd = ncomp == 0 ? 0.0 : dkr-nd(dkr-read(sts[il][3], ncomp * dql-hd(c)), dql-flat(lr[4]));
   let noted = nothing?(input) ? 0 : dql-noted(c, fal, il, pos, input, lr, heads);
   let mx1 = dql-max-all(fal, il, ta, nda);
   let mx2 = dql-max-all(fal, il, tf, ndf);
   let enq = record_set(fal, "enq-" ++ il.str() ++ "-" ++ pos.str(), [n1, n2]);
   // at the second ratio-4 emission the GPU's two compressed rows against the rows an UNSHIFTED state would give (the shift's witness)
   let ns = (dql-ratio(c, il) == 4 && ncomp == 2) ? record_set(fal, "ns-" ++ il.str() ++ "-" ++ pos.str(), dkr-nd(dkr-read(sts[il][3], 2 * dql-hd(c)), dql-flat(lr[8]))) : 0;
   let said = print_str("  " ++ label ++ " block " ++ il.str() ++ " pos " ++ pos.str() ++ " enq " ++ n1.str() ++ "+" ++ n2.str() ++ " ids " ++ ids.str() ++ "/" ++ refIds.str() ++ "  " ++ dql-labels(ta, nda) ++ dql-labels(tf, ndf) ++ (ncomp == 0 ? "" : "comp_rows " ++ compNd.str() ++ (compNd < 1.0e-12 ? "" : " differing " ++ dql-diffs(dkr-read(sts[il][3], ncomp * dql-hd(c)), dql-flat(lr[4]), 0, 1.0).str())));
   let flips = ncomp == 0 ? [] : dql-diffs(dkr-read(sts[il][3], ncomp * dql-hd(c)), dql-flat(lr[4]), 0, 1.0);
   // A cached row is rounded by fp8 and f16, and f32 and fp64 can land on opposite sides of a rounding boundary: when the rows differ in at most two elements and each by at most one f16 step
   // (a relative 2^-10 of that element), it is such a flip and not a kernel defect, and the stages after it are held to the chain bound instead of the floor (the flip is printed).
   let flipOk = len(flips) > 0 && len(flips) <= 2 && dql-one-step?(flips);
   let bound = flipOk ? dql-chain-bound() : dkr-floor();
   fed && !nothing?(n1) && !nothing?(n2) && ids == refIds && dql-below(nda, bound) && dql-below(ndf, bound) && (compNd < dkr-floor() || flipOk);
  }
  // the largest disagreement each stage of each block reaches over the eight alone positions (key "max-<block>-<stage>"), and the chained output streams ("max-chain-<block>")
  def dql-max-set(fal, key, v) = record_set(fal, key, (record_has(fal, key) && record_get(fal, key) >= v) ? record_get(fal, key) : v);
  def dql-max-all(fal, il, ts, nds) = len(ts) == 0 ? 0 : { let s = dql-max-set(fal, "max-" ++ il.str() ++ "-" ++ ts[0][0], nds[0]); dql-max-all(fal, il, ts[1:], nds[1:]); };
  def dql-stage-labels() = ["xn", "q", "kv", "heads", "low", "attn_out", "after_attn", "ffn_cur", "ffn_norm", "logits", "w", "shared", "ffn_out", "out_hc"];
  def dql-maxes-line(fal, il, labels) = len(labels) == 0 ? "" : (labels[0] ++ " " ++ record_get(fal, "max-" ++ il.str() ++ "-" ++ labels[0]).str() ++ "  " ++ dql-maxes-line(fal, il, labels[1:]));
  def dql-print-maxes(fal) {
   let a = print_str("  stage maxima block 0: " ++ dql-maxes-line(fal, 0, dql-stage-labels()));
   let b = print_str("  stage maxima block 1: " ++ dql-maxes-line(fal, 1, dql-stage-labels()));
   let c = print_str("  stage maxima block 2: " ++ dql-maxes-line(fal, 2, dql-stage-labels()));
   let d = print_str("  chained out_hc maxima: " ++ record_get(fal, "max-chain-0").str() ++ " " ++ record_get(fal, "max-chain-1").str() ++ " " ++ record_get(fal, "max-chain-2").str());
   1;
  }
  def dql-one-step?(flips) = len(flips) == 0 ? true : (dkr-abs(flips[0][1] - flips[0][2]) <= 0.00098 * (dkr-abs(flips[0][1]) > dkr-abs(flips[0][2]) ? dkr-abs(flips[0][1]) : dkr-abs(flips[0][2])) && dql-one-step?(flips[1:]));
  // the elements two vectors disagree on beyond a part in 1e9 of the larger's peak: [index, gpu, ref]
  def dql-diffs(a, b, i, peak) = (len(a) != len(b) || i == len(a)) ? [] : (dkr-abs(a[i] - b[i]) > peak * 1.0e-9 ? cons([i, a[i], b[i]], dql-diffs(a, b, i + 1, peak)) : dql-diffs(a, b, i + 1, peak));
  def dql-alone(c, ref, il, pos, sts, fal) = dql-run(c, "alone", il, pos, il == 0 ? nothing() : dql-input(ref, pos, il), dql-lr(ref, pos, il), sts, fal);

  // ---- 1: counts and refusals -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  def dql-enq(fal, il, pos) = record_get(fal, "enq-" ++ il.str() ++ "-" ++ pos.str());
  def dql-counts(fal) = dql-enq(fal, 0, 0) == [22, 19] && dql-enq(fal, 1, 0) == [25, 18] && dql-enq(fal, 1, 2) == [25, 18] && dql-enq(fal, 1, 3) == [31, 18] && dql-enq(fal, 2, 0) == [25, 18]
   && dql-enq(fal, 2, 1) == [30, 18] && dql-enq(fal, 2, 2) == [25, 18] && dql-enq(fal, 2, 3) == [30, 18]
   && dql-enq(fal, 0, 7) == [22, 19] && dql-enq(fal, 1, 4) == [25, 18] && dql-enq(fal, 1, 6) == [25, 18] && dql-enq(fal, 1, 7) == [31, 18]
   && dql-enq(fal, 2, 4) == [25, 18] && dql-enq(fal, 2, 5) == [30, 18] && dql-enq(fal, 2, 6) == [25, 18] && dql-enq(fal, 2, 7) == [30, 18];
  def dql-supported(c) = dkl-supported?(dql-ctx(c), 0) && dkl-supported?(dql-ctx(c), 1) && dkl-supported?(dql-ctx(c), 2) && !dkl-supported?(dql-ctx(c), 3) && !dkl-supported?(dql-ctx(c), 0 - 1);
  // a refusal answers nothing and leaves the output buffer as the caller left it
  def dql-refusals(c, sts) {
   let ctx = dql-ctx(c);
   let w = metal_buf_write(dso-buf(ctx, "resid-next"), 0, dkr-sentinel(4096));
   let a = dsv4-layer-attn(ctx, sts, 0, 8, 8);
   let b = dsv4-layer-attn(ctx, sts, 3, 0, 8);
   let d = dsv4-layer-attn(ctx, sts, 1, 2048, 4096);
   let e = dsv4-layer-ffn(ctx, 3, 5);
   let s = metal_sync();
   let after = dql-rd(ctx, "resid-next", 1024);
   nothing?(a) && nothing?(b) && nothing?(d) && nothing?(e) && after[0] > 1.0e15 && after[1023] > 1.0e15;
  }

  // ---- 32: chained -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  def dql-chain-layer(c, ref, il, pos, sts, fal) {
   let ctx = dql-ctx(c);
   let token = dql-tokens()[pos];
   let n1 = dsv4-layer-attn(ctx, sts, il, pos, 8);
   let n2 = dsv4-layer-ffn(ctx, il, token);
   let s = metal_sync();
   let nd = dkr-nd(dql-rd(ctx, "resid", 1024), dql-lr(ref, pos, il)[2]);
   let ids = dql-read-ids(ctx);
   let mx = dql-max-set(fal, "max-chain-" ++ il.str(), nd);
   let said = print_str("  chained block " ++ il.str() ++ " pos " ++ pos.str() ++ " out_hc nd " ++ nd.str() ++ " ids " ++ ids.str() ++ "/" ++ record_get(dql-lr(ref, pos, il)[1], "selected").str());
   !nothing?(n1) && !nothing?(n2) && nd < dql-chain-bound() && ids == record_get(dql-lr(ref, pos, il)[1], "selected");
  }
  def dql-chain-pos(c, ref, pos, sts, fal) {
   let ctx = dql-ctx(c);
   let fed = dql-embed-in(ctx, dql-tokens()[pos]);
   fed && dql-chain-layer(c, ref, 0, pos, sts, fal) && dql-chain-layer(c, ref, 1, pos, sts, fal) && dql-chain-layer(c, ref, 2, pos, sts, fal);
  }
  def dql-chain-from(c, ref, pos, sts, fal) = pos == len(dql-tokens()) ? true : (dql-chain-pos(c, ref, pos, sts, fal) && dql-chain-from(c, ref, pos + 1, sts, fal));
  def dql-chain(c, ref, sts, fal) = dql-chain-from(c, ref, 0, sts, fal);

  // ---- 64: the checks can fail -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  def dql-tilt(xs, i) = len(xs) == 0 ? [] : cons(xs[0] * (1.0 + ((i % 2) == 0 ? 0.0001 : 0.0 - 0.0001)), dql-tilt(xs[1:], i + 1));
  def dql-tilted(c, ref, sts) {
   let ctx = dql-ctx(c);
   let lr = dql-lr(ref, 0, 0);
   let w = dql-write-resid(ctx, dql-tilt(ref[0][0], 0));
   let n1 = dsv4-layer-attn(ctx, sts, 0, 0, 8);
   let n2 = dsv4-layer-ffn(ctx, 0, dql-tokens()[0]);
   let s = metal_sync();
   let nd = dkr-nd(dql-rd(ctx, "resid", 1024), lr[2]);
   let said = print_str("  tilted by 1e-4: block 0 pos 0 out_hc nd " ++ nd.str());
   !nothing?(n1) && !nothing?(n2) && nd > dkr-floor();
  }
  // the embedding path agrees with the reference's own embedding input
  def dql-embedding(c, ref) {
   let ctx = dql-ctx(c);
   let fed = dql-embed-in(ctx, dql-tokens()[0]);
   let s = metal_sync();
   fed && dql-rd(ctx, "resid", 1024) == ref[0][0];
  }
  def dql-far(fal, key) = record_has(fal, key) && record_get(fal, key) > 0.0001;
  def dql-witnessed(fal) = dql-far(fal, "nc-1-3") && dql-far(fal, "nc-2-1") && dql-far(fal, "nc-2-3") && dql-far(fal, "nc-1-7") && dql-far(fal, "nc-2-5") && dql-far(fal, "nc-2-7");
  // the second ratio-4 window reads the shifted state: the GPU's two compressed rows at position 7 are far from the rows an unshifted state would give (and equal the twin's, in the alone leg)
  def dql-shift-witnessed(fal) = dql-far(fal, "ns-1-7");

  // ---- 512: the clamp is wired per block and it bites -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  // the per-block clamp the fixture's metadata holds, and the one the layer cell reads from the header
  def dql-clamps-meta(c) = dfo-meta(record_get(c, "r"), "deepseek4.swiglu_clamp_exp");
  def dql-clamp-wired(c) {
   let ms = dql-clamps-meta(c);
   let ctx = dql-ctx(c);
   len(ms) == 3 && dkl-clamp(ctx, 0) == ms[0] && dkl-clamp(ctx, 1) == ms[1] && dkl-clamp(ctx, 2) == ms[2] && ms == [10.0, 1.0, 2.0] && dkl-clamp(ctx, 1) != dkl-clamp(ctx, 2);
  }
  // on the oracle's own activations at position 0 of block il: the first routed expert's mid and the shared expert's mid, clamped (the block's lim) against the clamp off; nd of the two
  def dql-bite(c, ref, il) {
   let f = dql-lr(ref, 0, il)[1];
   let lim = dkl-clamp(dql-ctx(c), il);
   let e = head(record_get(f, "per_expert"));
   let w = head(record_get(f, "expert_w"));
   let on = dnr-mid(e[1], e[2], w, lim);
   let off = dnr-mid(e[1], e[2], w, 0.0);
   let son = dnr-mid(record_get(f, "sh_gate"), record_get(f, "sh_up"), 1.0, lim);
   let soff = dnr-mid(record_get(f, "sh_gate"), record_get(f, "sh_up"), 1.0, 0.0);
   [dkr-nd(on, off), dkr-nd(son, soff), dkr-nd(e[3], on), dkr-nd(record_get(f, "sh_mid"), son)];
  }
  // ---- 1024: the type wiring can fail, on the layer's own dispatch path ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  // A copy of the emitted kernel text with one claim dropped, compiled fresh, is put in the context's pipeline record under the real kernel's name for one block run and the original put back: the block is
  // dispatched exactly as it is (dkl-dense, dkl-expert-kernel read the tensor's type and name the kernel), and the gate has to see the planted lane. The tree's text is not touched.
  def dql-replace(s, from, to) { let p = str_find(s, from, 0); p < 0 ? s : substring(s, 0, p) ++ to ++ substring(s, p + str_len(from), str_len(s)); }
  def dql-planted-run(c, ref, sts, name, pipe, il) {
   let ps = dso-ps(dql-ctx(c));
   let was = record_get(ps, name);
   let set1 = record_set(ps, name, pipe);
   let r = try dql-alone(c, ref, il, 0, sts, record_new(0)) catch false;
   let set2 = record_set(ps, name, was);
   r;
  }
  def dql-plants(c, ref, sts) {
   let ctx = dql-ctx(c);
   // THE PLANTS RIDE THE KERNELS THE LAYER NOW DISPATCHES (2026-10-03): the real file's down stack runs the four-row Q2_K lane, its gate and up the four-row IQ2_XXS lane, its dense Q8_0 ds4's Metal-order matvec
   // (dkr-unit-lanes), so the three mutations are made in THAT text and planted under THOSE names; the id kernels and the lane matvec are no longer on this path.
   let scale = metal_pipeline(dql-replace(dkr-unit-lanes(), "float ds = d * float(sc & 15u);", "float ds = d * float(sc / 16u);"), "form_dsv4_q2k_matvec_experts4_fast");
   let stride = metal_pipeline(dql-replace(dkr-unit-lanes(), "((ulong)r * (ulong)nb + (ulong)ib) * 34ul;", "((ulong)r * (ulong)nb + (ulong)ib) * 33ul;"), "form_dsv4_q80_matvec_ds4");
   let wrong = dso-pipe(ctx, "form_dsv4_iq2_matvec_experts4_fast");
   let control = dql-planted-run(c, ref, sts, "form_dsv4_q2k_matvec_experts4_fast", dso-pipe(ctx, "form_dsv4_q2k_matvec_experts4_fast"), 1);
   let a = dql-planted-run(c, ref, sts, "form_dsv4_q2k_matvec_experts4_fast", scale, 1);
   let b = dql-planted-run(c, ref, sts, "form_dsv4_q80_matvec_ds4", stride, 0);
   let w = dql-planted-run(c, ref, sts, "form_dsv4_q2k_matvec_experts4_fast", wrong, 1);
   let again = dql-planted-run(c, ref, sts, "form_dsv4_q2k_matvec_experts4_fast", dso-pipe(ctx, "form_dsv4_q2k_matvec_experts4_fast"), 1);
   let said = print_str("  plants: control " ++ control.str() ++ ", Q2_K scale mis-read " ++ a.str() ++ ", Q8_0 stride 33 " ++ b.str() ++ ", wrong type routed (the IQ2_XXS kernel on Q2_K) " ++ w.str() ++ ", restored " ++ again.str());
   scale > 0 && stride > 0 && control && !a && !b && !w && again;
  }
  // ---- 2048: an expert type no kernel reads is a refusal, never a neighbour's kernel ------------------------------------------------------------------
  // dkl-expert-kernel names the three kernels for 40, 16 and 10 and reads NOTHING for any other type. The plant: block 1's down stack's view retyped 12 (Q4_K: priced, with no id kernel) in the context's own
  // view record for one run and restored: dkl-supported? refuses the block, dsv4-layer-ffn answers nothing, dkl-experts (called directly, past admission) answers [0] and enqueues none of its four dispatches
  // (the expert buffers and the stream buffer keep their sentinel), and with the view restored the same calls read supported and four enqueues.
  def dql-kernel-names() = dkl-expert-kernel(40) == "form_dsv4_mx4_matvec_id" && dkl-expert-kernel(16) == "form_dsv4_iq2_matvec_id" && dkl-expert-kernel(10) == "form_dsv4_q2k_matvec_id"
   && nothing?(dkl-expert-kernel(12)) && nothing?(dkl-expert-kernel(41)) && nothing?(dkl-expert-kernel(8)) && nothing?(dkl-expert-kernel(0)) && nothing?(dkl-expert-kernel(0 - 1));
  def dql-sentinels(ctx) = metal_buf_write(dso-buf(ctx, "xgate"), 0, dkr-sentinel(16)) >= 0 && metal_buf_write(dso-buf(ctx, "xdown"), 0, dkr-sentinel(16)) >= 0 && metal_buf_write(dso-buf(ctx, "resid-next"), 0, dkr-sentinel(16)) >= 0;
  def dql-untouched?(ctx) = dql-rd(ctx, "xgate", 4)[0] > 1.0e15 && dql-rd(ctx, "xdown", 4)[0] > 1.0e15 && dql-rd(ctx, "resid-next", 4)[0] > 1.0e15;
  def dql-expert-refusal(c) {
   let ctx = dql-ctx(c);
   let vx = dso-vx(ctx);
   let name = "blk.1.ffn_down_exps.weight";
   let v = record_get(vx, name);
   let armed = dql-sentinels(ctx);
   let p1 = record_set(vx, name, [v[0], v[1], 12, v[3], v[4], v[5]]);
   let sup = dkl-supported?(ctx, 1);
   let ex = dkl-experts(ctx, 1);
   let f = dsv4-layer-ffn(ctx, 1, dql-tokens()[0]);
   let s1 = metal_sync();
   let held = dql-untouched?(ctx);
   let p2 = record_set(vx, name, v);
   let sup2 = dkl-supported?(ctx, 1);
   let ex2 = dkl-experts(ctx, 1);
   let s2 = metal_sync();
   let said = print_str("  expert type refusal: kernel names " ++ dql-kernel-names().str() ++ ", planted type 12: supported " ++ sup.str() ++ ", dkl-experts " ++ ex.str() ++ ", layer-ffn nothing " ++ nothing?(f).str() ++ ", buffers untouched " ++ held.str() ++ "; restored: supported " ++ sup2.str() ++ ", dkl-experts " ++ ex2.str());
   dql-kernel-names() && armed && !sup && ex == [0] && nothing?(f) && held && sup2 && ex2 == [1, 1, 1, 1];
  }
  def dql-clamp-bites(c, ref) {
   let b0 = dql-bite(c, ref, 0);
   let b1 = dql-bite(c, ref, 1);
   let b2 = dql-bite(c, ref, 2);
   let said = print_str("  clamp: block 0 (10.0) off-vs-on " ++ b0[0].str() ++ "/" ++ b0[1].str() ++ "  block 1 (1.0) " ++ b1[0].str() ++ "/" ++ b1[1].str() ++ "  block 2 (2.0) " ++ b2[0].str() ++ "/" ++ b2[1].str() ++ "  oracle's own mid vs this clamp " ++ b1[2].str() ++ "/" ++ b1[3].str());
   b0[0] == 0.0 && b0[1] == 0.0 && b1[2] < 1.0e-9 && b1[3] < 1.0e-9 && b2[2] < 1.0e-9 && b2[3] < 1.0e-9;
  }
 }
 let root = temp_dir() ++ "/dsv4-layer-q8q2-band-" ++ now_unix_ms().str();
 let path = root ++ ".gguf";
 let wrote = dfx-v-write(path);
 let r = dfo-open(path);
 let live0 = dvb-live();
 let mapped0 = dvb-mapped();
 let ctx = dsv4-open-span(path, 8, 1);
 let opened = len(ctx) == 13;
 let m = opened ? ctx[2] : nothing();
 let c = record_new(0, "r", r, "g", dfo-geometry(r), "m", m, "ctx", ctx);
 let prep = opened ? dsv4-prepare(ctx) : 0;
 let stsA = opened ? dsv4-new-state(m, ctx[0], 8) : nothing();
 let stsB = opened ? dsv4-new-state(m, ctx[0], 8) : nothing();
 let stsT = opened ? dsv4-new-state(m, ctx[0], 8) : nothing();
 let ref = dql-ref-start(c);
 let fal = record_new(0);
 let said = print_str("reference built: " ++ len(ref).str() ++ " positions");
 let r2 = try opened && dql-alone(c, ref, 0, 0, stsA, fal) && dql-alone(c, ref, 0, 1, stsA, fal) && dql-alone(c, ref, 0, 2, stsA, fal) && dql-alone(c, ref, 0, 3, stsA, fal)
  && dql-alone(c, ref, 0, 4, stsA, fal) && dql-alone(c, ref, 0, 5, stsA, fal) && dql-alone(c, ref, 0, 6, stsA, fal) && dql-alone(c, ref, 0, 7, stsA, fal) catch false;
 let r4 = try opened && dql-alone(c, ref, 1, 0, stsA, fal) && dql-alone(c, ref, 1, 1, stsA, fal) && dql-alone(c, ref, 1, 2, stsA, fal) catch false;
 let r8 = try opened && dql-alone(c, ref, 2, 0, stsA, fal) catch false;
 let r16 = try opened && dql-alone(c, ref, 1, 3, stsA, fal) && dql-alone(c, ref, 2, 1, stsA, fal) && dql-alone(c, ref, 2, 2, stsA, fal) && dql-alone(c, ref, 2, 3, stsA, fal) catch false;
 let r256 = try opened && dql-alone(c, ref, 1, 4, stsA, fal) && dql-alone(c, ref, 1, 5, stsA, fal) && dql-alone(c, ref, 1, 6, stsA, fal) && dql-alone(c, ref, 1, 7, stsA, fal)
  && dql-alone(c, ref, 2, 4, stsA, fal) && dql-alone(c, ref, 2, 5, stsA, fal) && dql-alone(c, ref, 2, 6, stsA, fal) && dql-alone(c, ref, 2, 7, stsA, fal) catch false;
 let c256 = dql-bit(r256, 256);
 let c512 = dql-bit(try opened && dql-clamp-wired(c) && dql-clamp-bites(c, ref) catch false, 512);
 let c2 = dql-bit(r2, 2);
 let c4 = dql-bit(r4, 4);
 let c8 = dql-bit(r8, 8);
 let c16 = dql-bit(r16, 16);
 let c1 = dql-bit(try opened && dql-supported(c) && dql-counts(fal) && dql-refusals(c, stsA) catch false, 1);
 let c32 = dql-bit(try opened && dql-chain(c, ref, stsB, fal) catch false, 32);
 let printed = try dql-print-maxes(fal) catch 0;
 let c64 = dql-bit(try opened && dql-witnessed(fal) && dql-shift-witnessed(fal) && dql-tilted(c, ref, stsT) && dql-embedding(c, ref) catch false, 64);
 let stsP = opened ? dsv4-new-state(m, ctx[0], 8) : nothing();
 let c1024 = dql-bit(try opened && dql-plants(c, ref, stsP) catch false, 1024);
 let c2048 = dql-bit(try opened && dql-expert-refusal(c) catch false, 2048);
 let left = opened ? dsv4-close(ctx, append(stsA, append(stsB, append(stsT, stsP)))) : [0];
 let c128 = dql-bit(try opened && len(left) == 0 && dvb-live() == live0 && dvb-mapped() == mapped0 catch false, 128);
 let removed = host_path_remove(path);
 print_str("dsv4-layer-q8q2-band claims " ++ c1.str() ++ " " ++ c2.str() ++ " " ++ c4.str() ++ " " ++ c8.str() ++ " " ++ c16.str() ++ " " ++ c32.str() ++ " " ++ c64.str() ++ " " ++ c128.str() ++ " " ++ c256.str() ++ " " ++ c512.str() ++ " " ++ c1024.str() ++ " " ++ c2048.str() ++ " unshifted " ++ (record_has(fal, "ns-1-7") ? record_get(fal, "ns-1-7").str() : "none") ++ " nocomp " ++ (record_has(fal, "nc-1-3") ? record_get(fal, "nc-1-3").str() : "none") ++ "/" ++ (record_has(fal, "nc-2-1") ? record_get(fal, "nc-2-1").str() : "none") ++ "/" ++ (record_has(fal, "nc-2-3") ? record_get(fal, "nc-2-3").str() : "none") ++ " live " ++ live0.str() ++ "/" ++ dvb-live().str() ++ " mapped " ++ mapped0.str() ++ "/" ++ dvb-mapped().str() ++ " removed " ++ removed.str());
 c1 + c2 + c4 + c8 + c16 + c32 + c64 + c128 + c256 + c512 + c1024 + c2048;
}
